{"design":"Stop-loss test: does putting a stop under each stock improve results?\n\nSet-up (the classic design from the stop-loss literature, e.g. Lei & Li 2009,\nKaminski & Lo 2014): every stock gets an equal slice of money and starts\nfully invested. Each slice then follows one exit rule. After a stop-out the\nslice sits in T-bills until its re-entry rule says buy again. The benchmark is\nthe same slices with no stop at all (buy and hold).\n\nFills:\n* Intraday stops (fixed %, trailing %, ATR at entry) act like a resting stop\n  order: if the day's low reaches the stop, the sale fills at the stop price,\n  or at the open if the stock gaps below it (so gap losses are counted).\n* Close-based stops (moving averages, chandelier, time stop) are decided at\n  the close and sold at the next open.\nEvery buy and sell pays 10 basis points. Nothing looks ahead.\n\nRun:  python -m stockanalysis.validation.stops\n","cells":["train_2003_2014","train_2015_now","holdout_2003_2014","holdout_2015_now","exam_2003_2014","exam_2015_now"],"results":[{"name":"No stop (buy and hold)","family":"Benchmark","kind":"none","reentry":"none","cells":{"train_2003_2014":{"total_return_pct":455.2,"cagr_pct":15.36,"volatility_pct":20.3,"sharpe":0.74,"max_drawdown_pct":-51.9,"return_to_drawdown":0.3,"years":12.0,"stocks":72,"invested_pct":100.0,"stop_outs":0,"stop_outs_per_stock_year":0.0,"rose_after_stop_pct":null,"avg_move_60d_after_stop_pct":null},"train_2015_now":{"total_return_pct":891.8,"cagr_pct":21.3,"volatility_pct":24.9,"sharpe":0.82,"max_drawdown_pct":-38.4,"return_to_drawdown":0.55,"years":11.9,"stocks":73,"invested_pct":100.0,"stop_outs":0,"stop_outs_per_stock_year":0.0,"rose_after_stop_pct":null,"avg_move_60d_after_stop_pct":null},"holdout_2003_2014":{"total_return_pct":424.4,"cagr_pct":14.82,"volatility_pct":21.1,"sharpe":0.7,"max_drawdown_pct":-54.3,"return_to_drawdown":0.27,"years":12.0,"stocks":57,"invested_pct":100.0,"stop_outs":0,"stop_outs_per_stock_year":0.0,"rose_after_stop_